===persian===

من از تو سیر نخواهم شد...
کویر از باران...
صدای ساز عثمان می‌آید...
من از تو سیر نخواهم شد...
کویر تشنهٔ باران است...
ببین که می‌آید...
صدای خسته عطشان...
صدایِ عثمان است...
۱۳۶۸/۱۱/۲۹

===machine===

I will never have my fill of you...
nor the desert of rain...
The sound of Osman's saz is coming...
I will never have my fill of you...
The desert thirsts for rain...
Look — it is coming...
the tired, parched voice...
it is the voice of Osman...
1368/11/29

===lantern===

I will never have my fill of you...
nor the desert of rain...
The sound of Osman's saz is coming...
I will never have my fill of you...
The desert is thirsty for rain...
Look — it is coming,
the tired, thirsting sound...
It is the sound of Osman.

1368/11/29

===translation===

===footnotes===

The poem turns on a rhyme English cannot keep: عطشان (*atshân*, thirsting) and
عثمان (*Osmân*) are one sound apart, so the parched voice the desert is waiting for and the name of
the man playing it arrive as very nearly the same word. Osman of Khaf, in eastern Khorasan, is also
the dotar player the dream-Alizadeh names in the letter twenty pages earlier.

